{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi1URwSibTGUNkdNZfVr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GmiAM5m8gfWXduyq71z4CL","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-070011__xa7e588/work/PLAN.md","offset":475,"limit":420},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10637,"cache_read_input_tokens":31820,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10637},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5f6aeda2-f9ed-42d4-a150-3a2efde4ea9e","uuid":"4c4d0c43-a223-406a-9dce-e2c7c2424109","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:00:28.856Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi1URephfMMpXH6E6EaC","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01GmiAM5m8gfWXduyq71z4CL":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-070011__xa7e588/work/PLAN.md","offset":475,"limit":420}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GmiAM5m8gfWXduyq71z4CL","type":"tool_result","content":"475\t                       ⇄ (deadBall → dropOut → play)\n476\t          → try → celebrate [→ replay] → conversion → kickoff (the scoring team kicks off)\n477\t          → dropGoal | penaltyGoal → kickoff\n478\thooter → (next stoppage) → halftime → kickoff (2nd half, other team) → hooter → fulltime | suddenDeath → results\n479\t```\n480\t\n481\t- Halves: `halfLength` = 120 s of **running** clock (stops at stoppages: set-piece setups, conversions, penalties,\n482\t  celebrations, replays, cutscenes). The TV clock shows sevens time, 0:00 to 7:00 per half (`shown = run × 420 /\n483\t  halfLength`). Settings: 2 / 3 / 4 / 5 minute halves (120 / 180 / 240 / 300 s).\n484\t- At zero: the HOOTER sounds; the half ends at the next stoppage (ball dead, a score, a tackle completed, a set piece\n485\t  awarded), so the last play is live. If open play runs 30 s past the hooter, the next tackle ends it.\n486\t- Kick-offs: the first half by the home team; the second by the away team; after any score, by the team that scored.\n487\t- Level at full time in the cup or with \"Sudden death\" on: SUDDEN DEATH extra time, the first score of any kind wins\n488\t  (\"GOLDEN POINT\"); if 120 s pass with no score in Exhibition, it's a draw; in the cup it goes on.\n489\t- Halftime: a 6-8 s dressing-room overlay (the coach's line in the cup, the stats in Exhibition); ends on ✕.\n490\t\n491\t### 7.2 Players, movement, turbo and control\n492\t\n493\t- **Roles** (sevens): PROP (loosehead), HOOKER, PROP (tighthead): the forwards; SCRUM-HALF, FLY-HALF, CENTRE, WING: the\n494\t  backs. The scrum-half takes the ball from rucks and scrums; the fly-half takes kick-offs and set kicks; the hooker\n495\t  throws lineouts; forwards form scrums and lineouts.\n496\t- **Stats** 1-10: SPD, POW, HND (hands), KCK, TKL. Derived: top speed `runSpeed × (0.8 + 0.04 × SPD)`; acceleration\n497\t  `accel × (1.15 - 0.03 × POW)`; turning at 10 rad/s (8 with the ball).\n498\t- **Movement:** an `E.Body` (`r` 5, `friction` 0, `gravity` 700) per player; velocity approaches `intent.move × speed`\n499\t  at the acceleration; carrying the ball costs 4% speed; mud costs 20% (§7.18).\n500\t- **Turbo:** held, it multiplies speed by `turboMult` (1.45) and drains a 3.0 s tank; it refills at 0.3 tank per second\n501\t  after 0.6 s of not using it. Turbo also adds 10% to tackle and fend strength and, with the ball, 5% to the chance a\n502\t  tackle breaks. Empty: it sputters (no effect, a puff sound).\n503\t- **States** (`st`): `idle, run, carry, pass, kick, sidestep, spin, fend, charge, tackling, diving, tackled, ground,\n504\t  getUp, stunned, ruck, scrum, lineout, lift, celebrate, binned, sentOff, walkout`. Each has its own timer `stT`. Only\n505\t  `idle/run/carry/charge` accept movement intents.\n506\t- **Control and switching:** each human seat drives one player of its team.\n507\t  - The team gains the ball: the seat takes the carrier (if two humans share a team, the one whose player is nearer).\n508\t  - Defending: Assisted auto-switch (§6.5); L1/R1 move control to the next teammate up/down the screen; ○ to the one\n509\t    nearest the ball; a mouse click on a teammate. Never onto a player held by another seat, in the sin bin, or on the\n510\t    ground.\n511\t  - Controlled players show a ring under their feet and a chevron with the seat label (P1-P4, or the hub name) in the\n512\t    seat colour.\n513\t\n514\t### 7.3 The ball\n515\t\n516\t- States: `held` (carried; drawn at the carry hand), `pass` and `kick` (in flight), `loose` (rolling or bouncing),\n517\t  `dead` (stoppage), `placed` (in a ruck, on the tee, at the scrum feed).\n518\t- Physics: an `E.Body` (`r` 3, `gravity` 600, `bounce` 0.45) updated with the map, so it bounces off the stands'\n519\t  walls as the sports kit's ball does off its boards (on the field there are no walls: out of play is decided by the\n520\t  lines, below); air drag 0.3/s; rolling friction 1.4/s; wind (§7.18) pushes it while airborne.\n521\t- **The oval bounce** (the soul of loose-ball chaos): on each ground contact with vertical speed above 30, rotate its\n522\t  ground velocity by `±U(0, 70°) × bounceChaos` and scale its rebound height by `U(0.3, 1.25)`; a grubber bounces\n523\t  higher at random (\"sat up nicely\"); all from `TT.rng`. Spin (end over end for kicks, spiral for passes) is drawn from\n524\t  `ball.rot`.\n525\t- Out of play: the ball's centre crossing a touchline (or the carrier's feet touching one) is **touch** → lineout to the\n526\t  team that did not touch it last, at the x where it crossed (moved 51 u from the try lines). Crossing a dead-ball line\n527\t  or touch-in-goal: if the attackers put it there → **22 drop-out** to the defenders; if the defenders did and it was\n528\t  not a kick from in-goal → 5 m scrum to the attackers.\n529\t- Pick-up: a loose ball below z 9 within 9 u of a player whose state accepts it (and 4.5 u if it moves faster than\n530\t  210) is gathered; at full sprint 15% are fumbled forward (a knock-on) unless HND ≥ 8.\n531\t\n532\t### 7.4 Passing\n533\t\n534\t- **Who receives:** legal receivers are teammates not in front of the passer (`(rx - px) × dir ≤ 4`), within 220 u,\n535\t  standing and not binned. L1 picks among those above the passer (smaller y), R1 among those below. Tap: the nearest by\n536\t  `|dy|` within 110 u (short pass). Hold more than 0.25 s: the second-nearest on that side, or the nearest if he is the\n537\t  only one (long pass, 300 u/s).\n538\t- **Flight:** aim at the receiver's lead point `rx + rvx × t × 0.9` (t from distance / speed), launched with\n539\t  `E.arc(..., { apex: 6 })` for short, `apex: 10` long; 230 u/s short.\n540\t- **Catch:** in the receiver's 10 u reach and below z 30: chance = `catchBase × (0.9 + 0.01 × HND)`, minus 0.06 for a\n541\t  long pass, minus `pressurePenalty` (0.12) with a defender within 20 u, minus 0.06 in rain; Grease Jersey and Iron\n542\t  Shoulders do not change it; a pass from or to a player ON FIRE is always caught. A miss either drops forward\n543\t  (knock-on) or spills loose (50/50 by the ball's direction).\n544\t- **Forward pass:** judged as the law does, relative to the passer: if `(ball velocity - passer velocity) · dir > 4\n545\t  u/s` at release, it is forward. The referee always calls it (whistle when caught or grounded): scrum to the other\n546\t  team. Only a mouse click on a man in front (or no assist) can throw one; the hover shows it red first.\n547\t- **Dummy:** a pass button with no legal receiver on that side (and pass assist off, or nobody anywhere) is a dummy:\n548\t  the carrier sells it; each defender within 40 u with eyes on the carrier \"buys it\" with 40% (turns toward the fake\n549\t  receiver for 0.3 s); +4 hype per defender sold.\n550\t- **Offload:** within the first 0.15 s of being tackled (not a big hit), L1/R1 pops a short pass to a legal receiver\n551\t  within 50 u; catch chance -0.1; +6 hype.\n552\t- **Interception:** a pass that flies within 10 u of an opponent below z 24 can be taken: the CPU tries with\n553\t  `0.15 × interceptMult`; a human holding ✕ near the lane (within 12 u) tries with 0.45. Success: the ball and +12 hype,\n554\t  and usually a long run.\n555\t\n556\t### 7.5 Running moves\n557\t\n558\t- **Sidestep (✕ with the ball):** an impulse of `sidestepPower` (140 u/s) perpendicular to the run toward the stick's\n559\t  side (no stick: away from the nearest defender), for `sidestepEvade` (0.25 s) any tackle attempt whiffs; cooldown\n560\t  0.6 s. A whiffed tackler stumbles (0.5 s). +6 hype when it beats a committed tackler.\n561\t- **Spin (✕ twice within 0.25 s):** 0.4 s evade, a full 360° body spin, 15% speed loss after; beats big hits too.\n562\t- **Fend (□ with the ball):** opens a 0.3 s `fendWindow` (the stiff arm out). A standard tackle arriving inside it\n563\t  fails with `fendBeat` (0.7) + 0.03 × (carrier POW - tackler TKL); a big hit fails with half that. A beaten tackler\n564\t  is shoved back 20 u and sits down (0.8 s). Cooldown 0.8 s. +6 hype.\n565\t- **Line break:** the carrier gets past the defensive line (every opponent but at most one, the deep sweeper, is now\n566\t  behind him, nearer his own try line): banner \"LINE BREAK!\", +8 hype, support runners turbo.\n567\t- **Grounding a try:** in the in-goal, ✕ dives and grounds (with style: +3 hype); otherwise the ball is grounded by\n568\t  itself after 2.5 s in the in-goal, when within 16 u of the dead-ball line, or when tackled there (always a try,\n569\t  arcade law). Running toward the posts before grounding makes the conversion easier: a real decision with the clock\n570\t  and the chasers.\n571\t\n572\t### 7.6 Kicking\n573\t\n574\t- **Grubber (tap ○):** along the ground 140-200 u ahead (stick aims within ±45°), `vz` 40, extra bounce chaos.\n575\t- **Punt (hold ○, release):** the meter fills in 0.9 s; while it fills the carrier runs straight on and the stick only\n576\t  aims. Distance `lerp(120, kickMax (520), power) × (0.75 + 0.03 × KCK)`; apex 60-110; aimed by the stick (forward\n577\t  cone ±70°; no stick: straight). Over 0.9 of the meter is the \"sweet spot\": +8% distance and true flight; outside, a\n578\t  random hook of up to ±(11 - KCK)°.\n579\t- **Bomb / up-and-under (punt with the stick pulled back at release):** apex 150, distance × 0.5; it hangs, and chasers\n580\t  can contest the catch (§7.11).\n581\t- **Kick to touch:** any punt aimed across a touchline goes out where it crosses: lineout to the other team (or to the\n582\t  kicking team from a penalty, §7.12).\n583\t- **Drop goal (hold ○ inside the opponents' 22, or within 300 u of their posts and facing them):** aimed at the posts\n584\t  (the stick nudges it ±8°); power and accuracy as a punt; good if it passes between the uprights above the crossbar:\n585\t  3 points. In that zone the stick pulled back at release still gives a bomb, and the stick pushed toward a touchline\n586\t  a cross-field punt; otherwise a held kick is the drop goal (the prompt says so: \"{b:ci} HOLD: DROP GOAL\").\n587\t- **Mouse:** right button hold and release kicks toward the cursor; the landing ring is drawn where it will come down at\n588\t  the current fill; the kind follows the same rules (in their 22 facing the posts: a drop goal).\n589\t- A landing marker (a pulsing ring decal) shows where every kick will come down, for both teams.\n590\t\n591\t### 7.7 Tackling\n592\t\n593\t- **Tackle (tap ✕ without the ball):** reaches 14 u (`tackleRange`) in front (within ±70° of facing). Chance =\n594\t  `tackleBase (0.78) × (0.9 + 0.02 × TKL - 0.02 × carrier POW)`, plus 0.1 from the side or behind, plus the\n595\t  difficulty bonus, minus 0.05 if the carrier is on turbo. Success: the paired `tackle` action (§11.2), then a ruck. Failure: \"broken\n596\t  tackle\": the tackler falls (0.6 s), the carrier staggers 0.4 s and goes on (+5 hype to the attack).\n597\t- **Big hit (hold ✕, let go in range):** charging takes `bigHitCharge` (0.7 s) to full; the charger moves at 1.15x and\n598\t  glows. Let go within 18 u: chance `0.7 + 0.2 × charge`. Full charge = **MONSTER HIT**: the carrier is launched\n599\t  (`bigHitLaunch`: 30-60 u back, z 20-40, a full flip), lands heavily and slides; the ball pops loose with\n600\t  `spillChance` (0.5), forward = knock-on; hit-stop 0.12 s, flash, shake 6, rumble, the crowd \"OOOOH\", a replay. Held\n601\t  past 1.2 s the charge goes red: a frontal hit then is a **high shot** (a foul, a yellow card if seen). A missed big\n602\t  hit sprawls the hitter for 1.0 s.\n603\t- **Dive tackle (□ without the ball):** a 0.35 s lunge of 30 u (`diveRange`); contact trips the carrier (an ankle tap:\n604\t  he falls forward, a tackle); a miss leaves the diver down for 1.2 s.\n605\t- **Gang tackle:** players with `immovable` (the boss, BIG UNIT; anyone in THUNDER RUN is simply unstoppable) are only\n606\t  \"held\" by the first successful tackle (they slow to 40% and drag the tackler); a second tackle within 1.0 s brings\n607\t  them down; otherwise they shrug it off after 1.2 s and the tackler is flung aside.\n608\t- **Cheap shot:** ✕ on an opponent without the ball (within 14 u) is a shoulder barge: the victim is flattened for\n609\t  1.6 s. It is a foul only if the referee sees it (§7.13). Unseen: +8 hype and Barry: \"The ref's missed that completely!\"\n610\t- **Collisions:** launched bodies hitting other players knock them down (1.0 s); hitting the referee is REF DOWN.\n611\t\n612\t### 7.8 The breakdown: ruck, jackal, \"use it\"\n613\t\n614\t- After a successful tackle the carrier goes to ground and places the ball behind him (toward his team). The ruck\n615\t  mark is the ball. The nearest two attackers and one or two defenders within 80 u commit (CPU); a human joins by\n616\t  running into the 16 u ruck zone (his player then locks into the ruck pose).\n617\t- **The contest** (`ruckTime`, 1.6 s): a tug-of-war bar from -1 (defence) to +1 (attack), starting at +0.2 + 0.1 ×\n618\t  (attackers - defenders committed). Each second each side adds 0.02 × the POW of its committed players. Mashing: a\n619\t  side with a human seat (its controlled player committed, or the tackled carrier) is driven by that seat's presses of\n620\t  ✕, each worth `mashWeight` (0.05), several humans adding up; a side with no human presses at `cpuMash` per second (±\n621\t  20%). Worked example, two attackers (POW 8 + 6) against one defender (POW 8): the commitment adds +0.12 a second, so a\n622\t  human who does not mash against a CPU at 9 presses a second ends at 0.3 + (0.12 - 0.45) × 1.6 = -0.23 (turnover); one\n623\t  mashing at 12 against a CPU at 6 ends at +0.97.\n624\t- **Jackal:** the first defender to reach the ball, if he arrives before any attacker and within 0.35 s of the tackle,\n625\t  may press □ to jackal: the bar swings -0.5 at once (\"JACKAL!\"). Pressing □ while not first is **hands in the ruck**: a\n626\t  foul if seen.\n627\t- **Result:** bar ≥ 0: the attacking scrum-half (or the nearest attacker) has the ball at the base; < 0: turnover, the\n628\t  defence picks it up and play goes on the other way. The attack's human seat switches to the receiver.\n629\t- **\"USE IT!\":** once the ball is at the base, the referee wants it out within 3 s (a countdown ring around the ball);\n630\t  if not, a scrum to the other team.\n631\t- **Offside line:** while a ruck is on, each team's offside line is its hindmost committed player's feet; a non-ruck\n632\t  player in front of his line who moves toward the ball when it comes out is offside (§7.13). The AI retreats; the HUD\n633\t  draws the line.\n634\t\n635\t### 7.9 Scrum\n636\t\n637\t- Awarded for a knock-on, a forward pass, an unplayable ruck (\"use it\"), not straight, the 5 m restarts. The mark: at\n638\t  least 51 u from touch and from the try lines. The non-offending team feeds.\n639\t- **Setup** (1.5 s): the three forwards each side bind (props either side of the hooker), scrum-halves at the side,\n640\t  backs line up 51 u behind the last feet.\n641\t- **Engage:** the referee calls **CROUCH** (0.6 s), **BIND** (0.6 s), **SET!** A ring closes on SET: ✕ within ±0.12 s\n642\t  = PERFECT (+0.25 on the push bar), ±0.25 s = GOOD (+0.1), later = nothing. Pressing before SET appears = **early\n643\t  engagement**: a free kick to the other team.\n644\t- **Push** (2.0 s): alternate L1 / R1 (Q / E): each alternating press adds `scrumPushWeight` (0.05); repeating a button\n645\t  counts half. The feeding team starts +0.15; each side adds 0.01 per second per POW point of its three forwards. CPU\n646\t  presses at its difficulty's rate.\n647\t- **Result:** the side with the bar on its side wins the ball at the scrum-half. Bar beyond 0.85: the losing scrum\n648\t  collapses (SCRUM PENALTY to the winners); if that winner is attacking within 50 u of the try line: **PUSHOVER TRY!**\n649\t  (5 points, grounded at the scrum's y, so converted from in line with it).\n650\t\n651\t### 7.10 Lineout\n652\t\n653\t- After touch. The line: three pods (FRONT, MIDDLE, BACK) 16 u apart from 51 u in from touch; each team's three\n654\t  forwards stand in their line, the throwing team's hooker throws.\n655\t- **Call** (up to 2.5 s): each side picks a pod: L1/R1 or up/down (or click a pod). The throwing team's call is shown\n656\t  only to its own players when the opponent is human on another device; on a shared screen, both are shown (honest\n657\t  couch play).\n658\t- **Throw:** ✕ stops a moving needle; in the green band = a good throw, in the edges = a wobbly one, outside = **NOT\n659\t  STRAIGHT** (scrum to the other team).\n660\t- **Jump:** the throwing team's jumper is lifted at its pod (lifters hoist him to z 60: \"INTO ORBIT!\"). If the defenders\n661\t  chose another pod, the throwers win it. If they chose the same pod, their jumper contests: attack score = 0.6 ×\n662\t  throw quality (0-1, from the needle) + 0.04 × jumper HND + 0.15; defence score = 0.6 × timing (1 - |press - arrival|\n663\t  / 0.3, clamped 0-1, from ✕ pressed as the ball arrives) + 0.04 × jumper HND; the higher score takes it (\"STOLEN!\").\n664\t  The winner taps it down to his scrum-half. CPU calls by weights (front .4, middle .35, back .25, never the same three\n665\t  times running); a CPU defence picks the right pod with its difficulty's read chance, and its timing error is drawn\n666\t  from its scrum timing σ.\n667\t\n668\t### 7.11 Kick-offs and 22 drop-outs\n669\t\n670\t- Kick-off from the centre spot by the fly-half (drop kick). The kicker aims a reticle (stick or mouse) on the\n671\t  receiving half and holds ○ (or the left mouse button) for power, letting go to kick. It must travel 102 u (\"10 m\"):\n672\t  short = \"NOT TEN!\" → a free kick to the receivers at halfway; straight into touch = a scrum to the receivers at\n673\t  halfway.\n674\t- Receivers catch automatically when the ball comes to a player in reach (10 u, z < 30). When a chaser and a receiver\n675\t  both reach a high ball, it's a **contest**: each presses ✕ as it arrives; the better timing (CPU: by difficulty and\n676\t  HND) takes it, the other is bumped down.\n677\t- 22 drop-out: the same, by the defending team from its own 22 line, distance unlimited.\n678\t\n679\t### 7.12 Tries, conversions, penalties, free kicks\n680\t\n681\t- **Try:** 5 points; celebration (each player has a celebration, §11.2), then a replay if earned (§7.20), then the\n682\t  conversion.\n683\t- **Conversion** (and **penalty goal**) set kick, in the behind-the-kicker camera:\n684\t  1. **Place:** move the tee back along the line through the grounding point parallel to touch (stick up/down, mouse\n685\t     drag or wheel), 51-400 u from the try line; the angle and the distance read out (\"38 M\").\n686\t  2. **Aim:** a reticle on the posts' plane, moved by the stick or the mouse; it sways a little (more for low KCK and\n687\t     higher difficulty); a windsock and arrow show the wind.\n688\t  3. **Power:** hold ○ (or the left mouse button) and let go: a meter needs to reach the distance's mark (shown); a\n689\t     tight accuracy band near the top adds no hook; elsewhere hooks up to ±(12 - KCK)°.\n690\t  4. **Flight:** the ball flies in 3D with the wind; it scores if it crosses the try line's plane between the uprights\n691\t     above the crossbar; hitting an upright is a DOINK (it bounces off, missed).\n692\t  A 20 s shot clock runs (the crowd's slow hand-clap speeds up). Conversion 2, penalty goal 3. CPU kicks are the same\n693\t  flight with an error drawn from its kicker's stats.\n694\t- **Penalty:** after a seen foul (and no advantage gained) the non-offending team's captain chooses on a big three-card\n695\t  screen (stick or mouse; CPU chooses by score, time and distance): **TAP & GO** (play restarts at once; the offenders\n696\t  are put 102 u back), **KICK AT GOAL** (if within 400 u; a set kick for 3), **KICK FOR TOUCH** (a punt aimed at the\n697\t  touchline; the kicking team throws in at the lineout).\n698\t- **Free kick** (early engagement, not ten): as a penalty, but no kick at goal.\n699\t- **Penalty try:** a seen foul against a carrier within 60 u of the try line with no defender between him and the line:\n700\t  7 points, no conversion.\n701\t\n702\t### 7.13 The referee and the laws he calls\n703\t\n704\t- **Referee Nigel Blewitt** is a Humanoid on the pitch (black kit, whistle). He runs to a spot 50 u behind the ball on\n705\t  the attacking side and 40 u toward the far touchline (so he never stands between play and the camera), at 95 u/s,\n706\t  steering round players; he turns to face the ball at 4 rad/s. His eyes: `E.sees(ref, offender, { range: refRange\n707\t  (260), fov: refFov (1.4) })` at the moment of the foul and again 0.3 s later. A \"Show the ref's view\" setting (default\n708\t  on) draws his `r.sightCone` faintly on the grass: the over-the-top tactic of fouling behind his back is part of the\n709\t  game.\n710\t- Always called (they are not about being seen): forward pass, knock-on, touch, not straight, early engagement, use it.\n711\t- Called only if seen: **high shot** (an over-charged frontal big hit): penalty + yellow card; **cheap shot** (a hit on\n712\t  a player without the ball): penalty, a yellow card for the same player's second; **offside** (a defender ahead of his\n713\t  offside line closing on the ball within 30 u when it comes out of a ruck, scrum or lineout): penalty; **hands in the\n714\t  ruck**: penalty.\n715\t- **Advantage:** a seen foul by team A while team B has the ball or a loose ball near it: the referee calls ADVANTAGE B\n716\t  (arm out) and play goes on; if B gains 100 u or scores within 5 s, ADVANTAGE OVER; if B loses the ball or 5 s pass\n717\t  without gain, play comes back for the penalty at the mark.\n718\t- **Cards and the sin bin:** a yellow card sends the player to the sin bin (the dumpster on the touchline) for `sinBin`\n719\t  (30 s of running clock); his team plays with six; the AI shape adapts. A second yellow for the same player is a red\n720\t  card: off for the match. A banner, the ref's card held high, the crowd boos, and a sad trombone.\n721\t- **Ref down:** a launched body, the chicken or a flying bystander hitting the referee floors him for 8 s: no fouls are\n722\t  called at all (cards, offside, cheap shots all free), \"REF DOWN! ANYTHING GOES!\", then he gets up and play goes on.\n723\t- The referee's calls appear as speech balloons over him (\"CROUCH!\", \"BIND!\", \"SET!\", \"USE IT!\", \"ADVANTAGE!\", \"PLAY\n724\t  ON!\", \"HANDS AWAY!\", \"PENALTY!\", \"KNOCK ON!\", \"FORWARD!\", \"NOT STRAIGHT!\") with his babble voice and arm signals.\n725\t\n726\t### 7.14 Scoring\n727\t\n728\t| Score | Points |\n729\t|---|---|\n730\t| Try (and pushover try) | 5 |\n731\t| Conversion | 2 |\n732\t| Penalty goal | 3 |\n733\t| Drop goal | 3 |\n734\t| Penalty try | 7 |\n735\t\n736\t### 7.15 Hype and supers\n737\t\n738\t- A HYPE meter per team (0-100), shown on the score bug. Gains (× `hypeMult`): tackle 4, broken tackle 5, sidestep or\n739\t  fend that beats a man 6, dummy 4 per man sold, offload 6, line break 8, big hit 10, monster hit 16, interception 12,\n740\t  jackal or ruck turnover 8, scrum won 6, lineout steal 8, try 15, conversion 5, drop goal 10, unseen cheap shot 8, air\n741\t  horn 40.\n742\t- Full: \"△ SUPER!\" flashes on the meter and over the team's controlled players.\n743\t- **THUNDER RUN** (△ with the ball): `superTime` (4 s); the carrier is on fire, 1.35x speed, unstoppable (tacklers\n744\t  bounce off and fly like skittles), the ball cannot be knocked loose; ends on a pass, a kick, a try or time.\n745\t- **HURRICANE HIT** (△ without the ball): the controlled defender locks onto the carrier and homes in at 2x speed for\n746\t  up to 2 s; contact is a guaranteed monster hit with the ball loose and everyone within 30 u knocked over; if the ball\n747\t  is passed first, it re-targets the new carrier once.\n748\t- CPU teams use supers: Thunder Run in the opponents' half with space ahead; Hurricane Hit when the opposing carrier is\n749\t  within 120 u of their try line.\n750\t\n751\t### 7.16 ON FIRE\n752\t\n753\tA player who scores two tries in a row (no opposing score between) is ON FIRE until the other team scores or 90 s pass:\n754\tunlimited turbo, passes and catches never fail, fends ×1.5, tackles on him ×0.6, kicks +20% distance, a flame trail\n755\t(emissive), a music layer, \"HE'S ON FIRE!\".\n756\t\n757\t### 7.17 Power-ups (thrown on by the crowd)\n758\t\n759\tEvery `powerupEvery` (30 ± 10 s) of open play a fan in the stand throws one onto the pitch (an `E.arc` from the crowd\n760\tto a spot at least 80 u from the ball); one at a time; it stays 15 s (blinking for the last 3). The first player to run\n761\tover it takes it. The CPU diverts one off-ball player if it is within 100 u.\n762\t\n763\t| Power-up | Looks | Effect |\n764\t|---|---|---|\n765\t| MEAT PIE | a steaming pie in a foil tray | turbo refilled and unlimited for 6 s |\n766\t| IRON SHOULDERS | riveted shoulder pads | 15 s: his tackles and fends always win; his hits are monster hits |\n767\t| MEGA BOOT | a golden boot with wings | his team's next kick: ×1.6 distance, on fire; a set kick's accuracy band ×2 (60 s) |\n768\t| GREASE JERSEY | a glistening jersey | 8 s: tackles on him fail 70% |\n769\t| AIR HORN | a red air horn | +40 hype for his team at once; the crowd goes barmy |\n770\t\n771\t### 7.18 Venues: weather and hazards (one twist each; data in §9.2)\n772\t\n773\t| Venue | Weather | Hazard |\n774\t|---|---|---|\n775\t| Muddington Park | rain (0.7) | **mud** patches (4-6 floor-tag blobs): speed ×0.8, acceleration ×0.6, tackles +10%, ball skids; catches -6% in rain; kits get muddier as the match goes on (rig colours mixed toward brown by each player's time in mud and on the ground) |\n776\t| Port Grumble Docks | gusty wind | **wind** that shifts every 15-25 s (strength 0-1, a windsock on the HUD) pushes airborne balls (40 u/s² × strength × `windMult`); **CAPTAIN CLUCKY**, the giant chicken mascot, invades every 50-70 s, runs across on an `E.Path` for about 6 s, bowling over everyone in his way (the carrier drops the ball), chased by the referee |\n777\t| The Furnace | clear night | **flame jets**: grates 32 u inside each touchline (8 a side) erupt in sequences; each glows orange for 1.0 s (the warning), then burns for 1.2 s; anyone within 12 u is TOASTED (stunned 1.2 s, smoking, briefly blackened; a toasted carrier drops the ball); fireworks on every try |\n778\t| The Megadome | thunderstorm (rain 0.9) | **lightning** every 20-30 s: a crackling ring (36 u) warns for 1.4 s at a spot 60-200 u from the ball, then a strike: a flash, thunder, a scorch decal; anyone inside is stunned 1.5 s (drawn as a skeleton for two frames: a shared `build: 'skeleton'` rig drawn in their place) and a carrier inside drops the ball |\n779\t\n780\t`hazardEvery` (×1.0) scales every hazard's frequency; 0 turns them off.\n781\t\n782\t### 7.19 AI\n783\t\n784\tBoth CPU teams and the CPU teammates of humans run the same brain; difficulty and the team's style (§9.1) change its\n785\tnumbers, never its logic. Shapes are recomputed every 0.25 s per team (staggered); decisions every 0.15 s plus the\n786\treaction delay.\n787\t\n788\t- **Attack shape** (team in possession; carrier at `(cx, cy)`, attacking direction `d`): six support slots in a\n789\t  staggered line behind the carrier, three each side: slot k at `(cx - d × (18 + 10k), cy ∓ 44k)` (spacing 44 to the\n790\t  open side, 36 to the blind side), clamped 20 u inside touch. Forwards take the k = 1 slots, backs the wider ones, the\n791\t  wing the widest open-side slot; then nearest-first; a reassignment needs a 20 u improvement (hysteresis). Supporters\n792\t  never stand in front of the carrier (they check stride to stay 6 u behind). After a line break they turbo.\n793\t- **Defence shape:** a line at `cx + d × 30` facing the attack (behind the offside line when there is one), defenders\n794\t  paired to attackers by y order (\"man on man drift\") so the line slides with the attack; the nearest defender by\n795\t  intercept time is the **tackler** (aims at the carrier's predicted position), the second the **cover** (20 u behind\n796\t  and inside); the **sweeper** (the wing or fly-half) sits 140 u deep at `lerp(cy, CY, .5)` to field kicks, and joins\n797\t  the line when the ball is within 200 u of his try line. With six men (sin bin) the line spaces wider.\n798\t- **Tackler decisions:** in range and facing, after `aiReaction`: try with `0.6 + 0.3 × aggression`; a big hit if POW\n799\t  ≥ 7 or aggression ≥ 0.6 and the carrier is coming head on (charging from 40 u out); a dive tackle when chasing a\n800\t  faster carrier from 18-30 u behind; cheap shots on the nearest support runner when the referee is not looking, with\n801\t  the team's `cheapShots` rate.\n802\t- **Carrier decisions** (CPU carriers, and the human's teammates when they have the ball): score each option and take\n803\t  the best, with noise by difficulty: run forward (space in a 30° cone ahead), pass to each legal receiver (his space\n804\t  minus defenders near the lane), sidestep (a tackler committing within 22 u: 25% × skill), fend (a tackler within 16 u\n805\t  and POW ≥ 6: 40%), kick (deep in his own 22 under pressure: to touch; behind a flat line with a fast chaser: grubber\n806\t  or chip; the last 20 s, trailing by 3 or less, in range: drop goal), dive in the in-goal (or run to the posts when no\n807\t  defender is within 60 u). Steer toward the widest gap in the defensive line; keep 20 u inside touch; turbo in space\n808\t  and when racing to the line; keep 30% of the tank.\n809\t- **Loose ball:** the two nearest from each team chase its predicted rest point; the rest keep their shape.\n810\t- **Kicks:** the receiving team's nearest (or the sweeper) goes to the landing marker, a second supports; the kicking\n811\t  team's two fastest chase. (There is no offside in open play in this game; this is deliberate.)\n812\t- **Set pieces:** see each set piece above. CPU kick-offs aim short and contestable, 120-200 u past halfway toward a\n813\t  touchline. CPU penalty choice: kick at goal within 300 u when the score is close or late; kick to touch from far; tap\n814\t  & go within 50 u of the line or when trailing late.\n815\t- **Difficulty** (the player's Settings choice shifts each cup opponent one step):\n816\t\n817\t| | Rookie | Pro | Legend |\n818\t|---|---|---|---|\n819\t| `aiReaction` | 0.40 s | 0.25 s | 0.14 s |\n820\t| Tackle chance | -0.12 | 0 | +0.08 |\n821\t| `cpuMash` | 6/s | 9/s | 12/s |\n822\t| Decision noise | 0.35 | 0.20 | 0.08 |\n823\t| Interception × | 0.5 | 1 | 1.5 |\n824\t| Scrum timing σ | 0.25 s | 0.12 s | 0.06 s |\n825\t| Early engagement | 8% | 3% | 0% |\n826\t| Lineout read | 0.25 | 0.35 | 0.45 |\n827\t\n828\t### 7.20 Instant replay\n829\t\n830\t- A ring buffer keeps the `MatchState` of the last 5 s at 60 Hz (every other step).\n831\t- Triggers: monster hits, supers, tries that came from a run of 200 u or more or beat a man, drop goals, pushover\n832\t  tries, interception tries; at most one replay in 30 s (tries always). Setting: Replays Big moments (default) / All\n833\t  tries / Off.\n834\t- Playback: the window from 2.5 s before to 1 s after the event, at 0.5x, through the normal presentation (states fed\n835\t  to the rigs), camera at zoom 1.35 on the key actor, letterbox bars, \"INSTANT REPLAY\" in the corner, Barry: \"Let's see\n836\t  that again!\"; any button skips. After a try it plays in the celebration, before the conversion. Never in AI Hub\n837\t  sessions.\n838\t\n839\t### 7.21 Stats and the Player of the Match\n840\t\n841\tPer team: possession % (time holding the ball), territory % (ball in the opponents' half), tries, conversions\n842\tmade/attempted, penalties conceded, tackles made/missed, big hits, monster hits, metres carried (`units / 10.24`), line\n843\tbreaks, turnovers won, offloads, cards. Player of the Match (winning side): tries × 10 + monster hits × 4 + tackles + metres\n844\t/ 10 + line breaks × 3 + turnovers × 3. Results show four tiles: TRIES, BIG HITS, METRES, POSSESSION.\n845\t\n846\t---\n847\t\n848\t## 8. Modes, scenes and flow\n849\t\n850\t```\n851\tboot → title ─(10 s idle)→ attract ─(any input)→ title\n852\t         │ PRESS START\n853\t         ▼\n854\t       menu ─(10 s idle)→ attract\n855\t         ├─ MEGA CUP ─→ cup hub ─→ story (prologue) → training (optional) → story (pre-match) → [join] → match\n856\t         │                 ▲                                                                        │\n857\t         │                 └──── results (win: next round; loss: CONTINUE? 10 s) ←───────────────────┘\n858\t         │                 final won → story (trophy) → story (third half) → credits → title\n859\t         ├─ EXHIBITION → join → setup (teams, venue, weather, time, halves) → match → results → rematch | menu\n860\t         ├─ TRAINING GROUND → drill list → match (drill) → next drill | list\n861\t         ├─ RECORDS → three tables (attract-style)\n862\t         ├─ SETTINGS → the standard settings screen (game.menu('settings'))\n863\t         └─ ABOUT & CREDITS → five pages\n864\tAI Hub session: boot → card (the game's own) → match (session) → end overlay (no title, no menus)\n865\t```\n866\t\n867\t| Scene | What it is |\n868\t|---|---|\n869\t| `title` | Night stadium under floodlights behind the logo; two Mudlarks passing a ball in the background (the real presentation, a tiny CPU loop); \"PRESS START\" (or the touch-only message); E.Arcade drives the idle cycle (`idle: 10`) |\n870\t| `menu` | BigMenu (scale 2): MEGA CUP (CONTINUE if a cup save exists), EXHIBITION, TRAINING GROUND, RECORDS, SETTINGS, ABOUT & CREDITS; a one-line description of the focused item; 10 s idle → attract |\n871\t| `attract` | the match scene with `{ attract: true }` (§13) |\n872\t| `cup` | the bracket: four big cards (ROUND ONE, QUARTER-FINAL, SEMI-FINAL, GRAND FINAL) with the opponent crest, venue, result or NEXT or LOCKED; PLAY NEXT MATCH, TRAINING, TEAM SHEET (seven portraits with nickname and role; ✕ on one shows its five stat bars), BACK |\n873\t| `story` | runs one `E.Story` node on a staged set (clubhouse, pitch-side, tunnel, podium; §9.3), then `go(next)`; ✕ turns pages, △ skips the scene |\n874\t| `join` | \"PRESS START TO JOIN\" (pads) or 2 (keyboard right half); each seat moves left/right to HOME, AWAY or CPU; in the cup only HOME; ✕ ready; up to 4 |\n875\t| `setup` | Exhibition: HOME and AWAY team cards (left/right to change; crest, name, three bars: SPEED, POWER, SKILL), VENUE (picture card), WEATHER (Venue default / Clear / Rain / Wind / Storm), TIME (Day / Dusk / Night), HALVES (2-5 min), SUDDEN DEATH (On/Off); PLAY |\n876\t| `match` | the match (pausable); data `{ home, away, venue, weather, time, half, cup, drill, attract, session, seed }` |\n877\t| `results` | the score with crests, PLAYER OF THE MATCH (portrait, two stats), four stat tiles, CONTINUE; a record set → initials (E.Arcade letter wheel) |\n878\t| `training` | the nine drills as big cards with a tick when done; ✕ plays one |\n879\t| `records` | three tables, one a page: BIGGEST WINS (margin), MOST TRIES IN A MATCH, BIGGEST HIT (metres flown); initials |\n880\t| `about` | five pages (§20); L1/R1 or left/right turns them |\n881\t| `credits` | rolls over the third half (§9.3), then the title |\n882\t| `card` | the AI Hub card (§15.2) |\n883\t\n884\t**Deep links** (for `tools/check.mjs`, filmstrips and screenshots, read from `location.hash` at start as the kits do):\n885\t`#title`, `#menu`, `#cup`, `#training`, `#training/<n>`, `#match` (an Exhibition with the defaults), `#match/<venue>`,\n886\t`#attract`, `#records`, `#about`, `#credits`, `#card` (the session card with made-up players, for screenshots only).\n887\t\n888\t**Pause menu** (standard, adjusted): Resume, RESTART MATCH, DEV MODE, Settings, Controls, Full screen, Quit to title\n889\t(none of these in a session, §15.2).\n890\t\n891\t**Saves:** `game.saves` with `menu: { saves: false }` (no manual save slots: arcade); the cup autosaves at the cup hub\n892\tand after each match: `{ round, results: [[home, away]], seeds, difficulty, stats }` with `place: 'MEGA CUP'`, `level:\n893\tround`. CONTINUE on the menu loads `game.saves.latest()`. Records and unlocks in `E.store` (`thugby:records`,\n894\t`thugby:unlocks`). Winning the cup unlocks the MEGACORP MAULERS in Exhibition and a BIG HEADS cheat (Settings, Game)."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5f6aeda2-f9ed-42d4-a150-3a2efde4ea9e","uuid":"afc6ceb6-1fca-4007-8846-e3645c8860dd","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:00:29.009Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-070011__xa7e588/work/PLAN.md","content":"                       ⇄ (deadBall → dropOut → play)\n          → try → celebrate [→ replay] → conversion → kickoff (the scoring team kicks off)\n          → dropGoal | penaltyGoal → kickoff\nhooter → (next stoppage) → halftime → kickoff (2nd half, other team) → hooter → fulltime | suddenDeath → results\n```\n\n- Halves: `halfLength` = 120 s of **running** clock (stops at stoppages: set-piece setups, conversions, penalties,\n  celebrations, replays, cutscenes). The TV clock shows sevens time, 0:00 to 7:00 per half (`shown = run × 420 /\n  halfLength`). Settings: 2 / 3 / 4 / 5 minute halves (120 / 180 / 240 / 300 s).\n- At zero: the HOOTER sounds; the half ends at the next stoppage (ball dead, a score, a tackle completed, a set piece\n  awarded), so the last play is live. If open play runs 30 s past the hooter, the next tackle ends it.\n- Kick-offs: the first half by the home team; the second by the away team; after any score, by the team that scored.\n- Level at full time in the cup or with \"Sudden death\" on: SUDDEN DEATH extra time, the first score of any kind wins\n  (\"GOLDEN POINT\"); if 120 s pass with no score in Exhibition, it's a draw; in the cup it goes on.\n- Halftime: a 6-8 s dressing-room overlay (the coach's line in the cup, the stats in Exhibition); ends on ✕.\n\n### 7.2 Players, movement, turbo and control\n\n- **Roles** (sevens): PROP (loosehead), HOOKER, PROP (tighthead): the forwards; SCRUM-HALF, FLY-HALF, CENTRE, WING: the\n  backs. The scrum-half takes the ball from rucks and scrums; the fly-half takes kick-offs and set kicks; the hooker\n  throws lineouts; forwards form scrums and lineouts.\n- **Stats** 1-10: SPD, POW, HND (hands), KCK, TKL. Derived: top speed `runSpeed × (0.8 + 0.04 × SPD)`; acceleration\n  `accel × (1.15 - 0.03 × POW)`; turning at 10 rad/s (8 with the ball).\n- **Movement:** an `E.Body` (`r` 5, `friction` 0, `gravity` 700) per player; velocity approaches `intent.move × speed`\n  at the acceleration; carrying the ball costs 4% speed; mud costs 20% (§7.18).\n- **Turbo:** held, it multiplies speed by `turboMult` (1.45) and drains a 3.0 s tank; it refills at 0.3 tank per second\n  after 0.6 s of not using it. Turbo also adds 10% to tackle and fend strength and, with the ball, 5% to the chance a\n  tackle breaks. Empty: it sputters (no effect, a puff sound).\n- **States** (`st`): `idle, run, carry, pass, kick, sidestep, spin, fend, charge, tackling, diving, tackled, ground,\n  getUp, stunned, ruck, scrum, lineout, lift, celebrate, binned, sentOff, walkout`. Each has its own timer `stT`. Only\n  `idle/run/carry/charge` accept movement intents.\n- **Control and switching:** each human seat drives one player of its team.\n  - The team gains the ball: the seat takes the carrier (if two humans share a team, the one whose player is nearer).\n  - Defending: Assisted auto-switch (§6.5); L1/R1 move control to the next teammate up/down the screen; ○ to the one\n    nearest the ball; a mouse click on a teammate. Never onto a player held by another seat, in the sin bin, or on the\n    ground.\n  - Controlled players show a ring under their feet and a chevron with the seat label (P1-P4, or the hub name) in the\n    seat colour.\n\n### 7.3 The ball\n\n- States: `held` (carried; drawn at the carry hand), `pass` and `kick` (in flight), `loose` (rolling or bouncing),\n  `dead` (stoppage), `placed` (in a ruck, on the tee, at the scrum feed).\n- Physics: an `E.Body` (`r` 3, `gravity` 600, `bounce` 0.45) updated with the map, so it bounces off the stands'\n  walls as the sports kit's ball does off its boards (on the field there are no walls: out of play is decided by the\n  lines, below); air drag 0.3/s; rolling friction 1.4/s; wind (§7.18) pushes it while airborne.\n- **The oval bounce** (the soul of loose-ball chaos): on each ground contact with vertical speed above 30, rotate its\n  ground velocity by `±U(0, 70°) × bounceChaos` and scale its rebound height by `U(0.3, 1.25)`; a grubber bounces\n  higher at random (\"sat up nicely\"); all from `TT.rng`. Spin (end over end for kicks, spiral for passes) is drawn from\n  `ball.rot`.\n- Out of play: the ball's centre crossing a touchline (or the carrier's feet touching one) is **touch** → lineout to the\n  team that did not touch it last, at the x where it crossed (moved 51 u from the try lines). Crossing a dead-ball line\n  or touch-in-goal: if the attackers put it there → **22 drop-out** to the defenders; if the defenders did and it was\n  not a kick from in-goal → 5 m scrum to the attackers.\n- Pick-up: a loose ball below z 9 within 9 u of a player whose state accepts it (and 4.5 u if it moves faster than\n  210) is gathered; at full sprint 15% are fumbled forward (a knock-on) unless HND ≥ 8.\n\n### 7.4 Passing\n\n- **Who receives:** legal receivers are teammates not in front of the passer (`(rx - px) × dir ≤ 4`), within 220 u,\n  standing and not binned. L1 picks among those above the passer (smaller y), R1 among those below. Tap: the nearest by\n  `|dy|` within 110 u (short pass). Hold more than 0.25 s: the second-nearest on that side, or the nearest if he is the\n  only one (long pass, 300 u/s).\n- **Flight:** aim at the receiver's lead point `rx + rvx × t × 0.9` (t from distance / speed), launched with\n  `E.arc(..., { apex: 6 })` for short, `apex: 10` long; 230 u/s short.\n- **Catch:** in the receiver's 10 u reach and below z 30: chance = `catchBase × (0.9 + 0.01 × HND)`, minus 0.06 for a\n  long pass, minus `pressurePenalty` (0.12) with a defender within 20 u, minus 0.06 in rain; Grease Jersey and Iron\n  Shoulders do not change it; a pass from or to a player ON FIRE is always caught. A miss either drops forward\n  (knock-on) or spills loose (50/50 by the ball's direction).\n- **Forward pass:** judged as the law does, relative to the passer: if `(ball velocity - passer velocity) · dir > 4\n  u/s` at release, it is forward. The referee always calls it (whistle when caught or grounded): scrum to the other\n  team. Only a mouse click on a man in front (or no assist) can throw one; the hover shows it red first.\n- **Dummy:** a pass button with no legal receiver on that side (and pass assist off, or nobody anywhere) is a dummy:\n  the carrier sells it; each defender within 40 u with eyes on the carrier \"buys it\" with 40% (turns toward the fake\n  receiver for 0.3 s); +4 hype per defender sold.\n- **Offload:** within the first 0.15 s of being tackled (not a big hit), L1/R1 pops a short pass to a legal receiver\n  within 50 u; catch chance -0.1; +6 hype.\n- **Interception:** a pass that flies within 10 u of an opponent below z 24 can be taken: the CPU tries with\n  `0.15 × interceptMult`; a human holding ✕ near the lane (within 12 u) tries with 0.45. Success: the ball and +12 hype,\n  and usually a long run.\n\n### 7.5 Running moves\n\n- **Sidestep (✕ with the ball):** an impulse of `sidestepPower` (140 u/s) perpendicular to the run toward the stick's\n  side (no stick: away from the nearest defender), for `sidestepEvade` (0.25 s) any tackle attempt whiffs; cooldown\n  0.6 s. A whiffed tackler stumbles (0.5 s). +6 hype when it beats a committed tackler.\n- **Spin (✕ twice within 0.25 s):** 0.4 s evade, a full 360° body spin, 15% speed loss after; beats big hits too.\n- **Fend (□ with the ball):** opens a 0.3 s `fendWindow` (the stiff arm out). A standard tackle arriving inside it\n  fails with `fendBeat` (0.7) + 0.03 × (carrier POW - tackler TKL); a big hit fails with half that. A beaten tackler\n  is shoved back 20 u and sits down (0.8 s). Cooldown 0.8 s. +6 hype.\n- **Line break:** the carrier gets past the defensive line (every opponent but at most one, the deep sweeper, is now\n  behind him, nearer his own try line): banner \"LINE BREAK!\", +8 hype, support runners turbo.\n- **Grounding a try:** in the in-goal, ✕ dives and grounds (with style: +3 hype); otherwise the ball is grounded by\n  itself after 2.5 s in the in-goal, when within 16 u of the dead-ball line, or when tackled there (always a try,\n  arcade law). Running toward the posts before grounding makes the conversion easier: a real decision with the clock\n  and the chasers.\n\n### 7.6 Kicking\n\n- **Grubber (tap ○):** along the ground 140-200 u ahead (stick aims within ±45°), `vz` 40, extra bounce chaos.\n- **Punt (hold ○, release):** the meter fills in 0.9 s; while it fills the carrier runs straight on and the stick only\n  aims. Distance `lerp(120, kickMax (520), power) × (0.75 + 0.03 × KCK)`; apex 60-110; aimed by the stick (forward\n  cone ±70°; no stick: straight). Over 0.9 of the meter is the \"sweet spot\": +8% distance and true flight; outside, a\n  random hook of up to ±(11 - KCK)°.\n- **Bomb / up-and-under (punt with the stick pulled back at release):** apex 150, distance × 0.5; it hangs, and chasers\n  can contest the catch (§7.11).\n- **Kick to touch:** any punt aimed across a touchline goes out where it crosses: lineout to the other team (or to the\n  kicking team from a penalty, §7.12).\n- **Drop goal (hold ○ inside the opponents' 22, or within 300 u of their posts and facing them):** aimed at the posts\n  (the stick nudges it ±8°); power and accuracy as a punt; good if it passes between the uprights above the crossbar:\n  3 points. In that zone the stick pulled back at release still gives a bomb, and the stick pushed toward a touchline\n  a cross-field punt; otherwise a held kick is the drop goal (the prompt says so: \"{b:ci} HOLD: DROP GOAL\").\n- **Mouse:** right button hold and release kicks toward the cursor; the landing ring is drawn where it will come down at\n  the current fill; the kind follows the same rules (in their 22 facing the posts: a drop goal).\n- A landing marker (a pulsing ring decal) shows where every kick will come down, for both teams.\n\n### 7.7 Tackling\n\n- **Tackle (tap ✕ without the ball):** reaches 14 u (`tackleRange`) in front (within ±70° of facing). Chance =\n  `tackleBase (0.78) × (0.9 + 0.02 × TKL - 0.02 × carrier POW)`, plus 0.1 from the side or behind, plus the\n  difficulty bonus, minus 0.05 if the carrier is on turbo. Success: the paired `tackle` action (§11.2), then a ruck. Failure: \"broken\n  tackle\": the tackler falls (0.6 s), the carrier staggers 0.4 s and goes on (+5 hype to the attack).\n- **Big hit (hold ✕, let go in range):** charging takes `bigHitCharge` (0.7 s) to full; the charger moves at 1.15x and\n  glows. Let go within 18 u: chance `0.7 + 0.2 × charge`. Full charge = **MONSTER HIT**: the carrier is launched\n  (`bigHitLaunch`: 30-60 u back, z 20-40, a full flip), lands heavily and slides; the ball pops loose with\n  `spillChance` (0.5), forward = knock-on; hit-stop 0.12 s, flash, shake 6, rumble, the crowd \"OOOOH\", a replay. Held\n  past 1.2 s the charge goes red: a frontal hit then is a **high shot** (a foul, a yellow card if seen). A missed big\n  hit sprawls the hitter for 1.0 s.\n- **Dive tackle (□ without the ball):** a 0.35 s lunge of 30 u (`diveRange`); contact trips the carrier (an ankle tap:\n  he falls forward, a tackle); a miss leaves the diver down for 1.2 s.\n- **Gang tackle:** players with `immovable` (the boss, BIG UNIT; anyone in THUNDER RUN is simply unstoppable) are only\n  \"held\" by the first successful tackle (they slow to 40% and drag the tackler); a second tackle within 1.0 s brings\n  them down; otherwise they shrug it off after 1.2 s and the tackler is flung aside.\n- **Cheap shot:** ✕ on an opponent without the ball (within 14 u) is a shoulder barge: the victim is flattened for\n  1.6 s. It is a foul only if the referee sees it (§7.13). Unseen: +8 hype and Barry: \"The ref's missed that completely!\"\n- **Collisions:** launched bodies hitting other players knock them down (1.0 s); hitting the referee is REF DOWN.\n\n### 7.8 The breakdown: ruck, jackal, \"use it\"\n\n- After a successful tackle the carrier goes to ground and places the ball behind him (toward his team). The ruck\n  mark is the ball. The nearest two attackers and one or two defenders within 80 u commit (CPU); a human joins by\n  running into the 16 u ruck zone (his player then locks into the ruck pose).\n- **The contest** (`ruckTime`, 1.6 s): a tug-of-war bar from -1 (defence) to +1 (attack), starting at +0.2 + 0.1 ×\n  (attackers - defenders committed). Each second each side adds 0.02 × the POW of its committed players. Mashing: a\n  side with a human seat (its controlled player committed, or the tackled carrier) is driven by that seat's presses of\n  ✕, each worth `mashWeight` (0.05), several humans adding up; a side with no human presses at `cpuMash` per second (±\n  20%). Worked example, two attackers (POW 8 + 6) against one defender (POW 8): the commitment adds +0.12 a second, so a\n  human who does not mash against a CPU at 9 presses a second ends at 0.3 + (0.12 - 0.45) × 1.6 = -0.23 (turnover); one\n  mashing at 12 against a CPU at 6 ends at +0.97.\n- **Jackal:** the first defender to reach the ball, if he arrives before any attacker and within 0.35 s of the tackle,\n  may press □ to jackal: the bar swings -0.5 at once (\"JACKAL!\"). Pressing □ while not first is **hands in the ruck**: a\n  foul if seen.\n- **Result:** bar ≥ 0: the attacking scrum-half (or the nearest attacker) has the ball at the base; < 0: turnover, the\n  defence picks it up and play goes on the other way. The attack's human seat switches to the receiver.\n- **\"USE IT!\":** once the ball is at the base, the referee wants it out within 3 s (a countdown ring around the ball);\n  if not, a scrum to the other team.\n- **Offside line:** while a ruck is on, each team's offside line is its hindmost committed player's feet; a non-ruck\n  player in front of his line who moves toward the ball when it comes out is offside (§7.13). The AI retreats; the HUD\n  draws the line.\n\n### 7.9 Scrum\n\n- Awarded for a knock-on, a forward pass, an unplayable ruck (\"use it\"), not straight, the 5 m restarts. The mark: at\n  least 51 u from touch and from the try lines. The non-offending team feeds.\n- **Setup** (1.5 s): the three forwards each side bind (props either side of the hooker), scrum-halves at the side,\n  backs line up 51 u behind the last feet.\n- **Engage:** the referee calls **CROUCH** (0.6 s), **BIND** (0.6 s), **SET!** A ring closes on SET: ✕ within ±0.12 s\n  = PERFECT (+0.25 on the push bar), ±0.25 s = GOOD (+0.1), later = nothing. Pressing before SET appears = **early\n  engagement**: a free kick to the other team.\n- **Push** (2.0 s): alternate L1 / R1 (Q / E): each alternating press adds `scrumPushWeight` (0.05); repeating a button\n  counts half. The feeding team starts +0.15; each side adds 0.01 per second per POW point of its three forwards. CPU\n  presses at its difficulty's rate.\n- **Result:** the side with the bar on its side wins the ball at the scrum-half. Bar beyond 0.85: the losing scrum\n  collapses (SCRUM PENALTY to the winners); if that winner is attacking within 50 u of the try line: **PUSHOVER TRY!**\n  (5 points, grounded at the scrum's y, so converted from in line with it).\n\n### 7.10 Lineout\n\n- After touch. The line: three pods (FRONT, MIDDLE, BACK) 16 u apart from 51 u in from touch; each team's three\n  forwards stand in their line, the throwing team's hooker throws.\n- **Call** (up to 2.5 s): each side picks a pod: L1/R1 or up/down (or click a pod). The throwing team's call is shown\n  only to its own players when the opponent is human on another device; on a shared screen, both are shown (honest\n  couch play).\n- **Throw:** ✕ stops a moving needle; in the green band = a good throw, in the edges = a wobbly one, outside = **NOT\n  STRAIGHT** (scrum to the other team).\n- **Jump:** the throwing team's jumper is lifted at its pod (lifters hoist him to z 60: \"INTO ORBIT!\"). If the defenders\n  chose another pod, the throwers win it. If they chose the same pod, their jumper contests: attack score = 0.6 ×\n  throw quality (0-1, from the needle) + 0.04 × jumper HND + 0.15; defence score = 0.6 × timing (1 - |press - arrival|\n  / 0.3, clamped 0-1, from ✕ pressed as the ball arrives) + 0.04 × jumper HND; the higher score takes it (\"STOLEN!\").\n  The winner taps it down to his scrum-half. CPU calls by weights (front .4, middle .35, back .25, never the same three\n  times running); a CPU defence picks the right pod with its difficulty's read chance, and its timing error is drawn\n  from its scrum timing σ.\n\n### 7.11 Kick-offs and 22 drop-outs\n\n- Kick-off from the centre spot by the fly-half (drop kick). The kicker aims a reticle (stick or mouse) on the\n  receiving half and holds ○ (or the left mouse button) for power, letting go to kick. It must travel 102 u (\"10 m\"):\n  short = \"NOT TEN!\" → a free kick to the receivers at halfway; straight into touch = a scrum to the receivers at\n  halfway.\n- Receivers catch automatically when the ball comes to a player in reach (10 u, z < 30). When a chaser and a receiver\n  both reach a high ball, it's a **contest**: each presses ✕ as it arrives; the better timing (CPU: by difficulty and\n  HND) takes it, the other is bumped down.\n- 22 drop-out: the same, by the defending team from its own 22 line, distance unlimited.\n\n### 7.12 Tries, conversions, penalties, free kicks\n\n- **Try:** 5 points; celebration (each player has a celebration, §11.2), then a replay if earned (§7.20), then the\n  conversion.\n- **Conversion** (and **penalty goal**) set kick, in the behind-the-kicker camera:\n  1. **Place:** move the tee back along the line through the grounding point parallel to touch (stick up/down, mouse\n     drag or wheel), 51-400 u from the try line; the angle and the distance read out (\"38 M\").\n  2. **Aim:** a reticle on the posts' plane, moved by the stick or the mouse; it sways a little (more for low KCK and\n     higher difficulty); a windsock and arrow show the wind.\n  3. **Power:** hold ○ (or the left mouse button) and let go: a meter needs to reach the distance's mark (shown); a\n     tight accuracy band near the top adds no hook; elsewhere hooks up to ±(12 - KCK)°.\n  4. **Flight:** the ball flies in 3D with the wind; it scores if it crosses the try line's plane between the uprights\n     above the crossbar; hitting an upright is a DOINK (it bounces off, missed).\n  A 20 s shot clock runs (the crowd's slow hand-clap speeds up). Conversion 2, penalty goal 3. CPU kicks are the same\n  flight with an error drawn from its kicker's stats.\n- **Penalty:** after a seen foul (and no advantage gained) the non-offending team's captain chooses on a big three-card\n  screen (stick or mouse; CPU chooses by score, time and distance): **TAP & GO** (play restarts at once; the offenders\n  are put 102 u back), **KICK AT GOAL** (if within 400 u; a set kick for 3), **KICK FOR TOUCH** (a punt aimed at the\n  touchline; the kicking team throws in at the lineout).\n- **Free kick** (early engagement, not ten): as a penalty, but no kick at goal.\n- **Penalty try:** a seen foul against a carrier within 60 u of the try line with no defender between him and the line:\n  7 points, no conversion.\n\n### 7.13 The referee and the laws he calls\n\n- **Referee Nigel Blewitt** is a Humanoid on the pitch (black kit, whistle). He runs to a spot 50 u behind the ball on\n  the attacking side and 40 u toward the far touchline (so he never stands between play and the camera), at 95 u/s,\n  steering round players; he turns to face the ball at 4 rad/s. His eyes: `E.sees(ref, offender, { range: refRange\n  (260), fov: refFov (1.4) })` at the moment of the foul and again 0.3 s later. A \"Show the ref's view\" setting (default\n  on) draws his `r.sightCone` faintly on the grass: the over-the-top tactic of fouling behind his back is part of the\n  game.\n- Always called (they are not about being seen): forward pass, knock-on, touch, not straight, early engagement, use it.\n- Called only if seen: **high shot** (an over-charged frontal big hit): penalty + yellow card; **cheap shot** (a hit on\n  a player without the ball): penalty, a yellow card for the same player's second; **offside** (a defender ahead of his\n  offside line closing on the ball within 30 u when it comes out of a ruck, scrum or lineout): penalty; **hands in the\n  ruck**: penalty.\n- **Advantage:** a seen foul by team A while team B has the ball or a loose ball near it: the referee calls ADVANTAGE B\n  (arm out) and play goes on; if B gains 100 u or scores within 5 s, ADVANTAGE OVER; if B loses the ball or 5 s pass\n  without gain, play comes back for the penalty at the mark.\n- **Cards and the sin bin:** a yellow card sends the player to the sin bin (the dumpster on the touchline) for `sinBin`\n  (30 s of running clock); his team plays with six; the AI shape adapts. A second yellow for the same player is a red\n  card: off for the match. A banner, the ref's card held high, the crowd boos, and a sad trombone.\n- **Ref down:** a launched body, the chicken or a flying bystander hitting the referee floors him for 8 s: no fouls are\n  called at all (cards, offside, cheap shots all free), \"REF DOWN! ANYTHING GOES!\", then he gets up and play goes on.\n- The referee's calls appear as speech balloons over him (\"CROUCH!\", \"BIND!\", \"SET!\", \"USE IT!\", \"ADVANTAGE!\", \"PLAY\n  ON!\", \"HANDS AWAY!\", \"PENALTY!\", \"KNOCK ON!\", \"FORWARD!\", \"NOT STRAIGHT!\") with his babble voice and arm signals.\n\n### 7.14 Scoring\n\n| Score | Points |\n|---|---|\n| Try (and pushover try) | 5 |\n| Conversion | 2 |\n| Penalty goal | 3 |\n| Drop goal | 3 |\n| Penalty try | 7 |\n\n### 7.15 Hype and supers\n\n- A HYPE meter per team (0-100), shown on the score bug. Gains (× `hypeMult`): tackle 4, broken tackle 5, sidestep or\n  fend that beats a man 6, dummy 4 per man sold, offload 6, line break 8, big hit 10, monster hit 16, interception 12,\n  jackal or ruck turnover 8, scrum won 6, lineout steal 8, try 15, conversion 5, drop goal 10, unseen cheap shot 8, air\n  horn 40.\n- Full: \"△ SUPER!\" flashes on the meter and over the team's controlled players.\n- **THUNDER RUN** (△ with the ball): `superTime` (4 s); the carrier is on fire, 1.35x speed, unstoppable (tacklers\n  bounce off and fly like skittles), the ball cannot be knocked loose; ends on a pass, a kick, a try or time.\n- **HURRICANE HIT** (△ without the ball): the controlled defender locks onto the carrier and homes in at 2x speed for\n  up to 2 s; contact is a guaranteed monster hit with the ball loose and everyone within 30 u knocked over; if the ball\n  is passed first, it re-targets the new carrier once.\n- CPU teams use supers: Thunder Run in the opponents' half with space ahead; Hurricane Hit when the opposing carrier is\n  within 120 u of their try line.\n\n### 7.16 ON FIRE\n\nA player who scores two tries in a row (no opposing score between) is ON FIRE until the other team scores or 90 s pass:\nunlimited turbo, passes and catches never fail, fends ×1.5, tackles on him ×0.6, kicks +20% distance, a flame trail\n(emissive), a music layer, \"HE'S ON FIRE!\".\n\n### 7.17 Power-ups (thrown on by the crowd)\n\nEvery `powerupEvery` (30 ± 10 s) of open play a fan in the stand throws one onto the pitch (an `E.arc` from the crowd\nto a spot at least 80 u from the ball); one at a time; it stays 15 s (blinking for the last 3). The first player to run\nover it takes it. The CPU diverts one off-ball player if it is within 100 u.\n\n| Power-up | Looks | Effect |\n|---|---|---|\n| MEAT PIE | a steaming pie in a foil tray | turbo refilled and unlimited for 6 s |\n| IRON SHOULDERS | riveted shoulder pads | 15 s: his tackles and fends always win; his hits are monster hits |\n| MEGA BOOT | a golden boot with wings | his team's next kick: ×1.6 distance, on fire; a set kick's accuracy band ×2 (60 s) |\n| GREASE JERSEY | a glistening jersey | 8 s: tackles on him fail 70% |\n| AIR HORN | a red air horn | +40 hype for his team at once; the crowd goes barmy |\n\n### 7.18 Venues: weather and hazards (one twist each; data in §9.2)\n\n| Venue | Weather | Hazard |\n|---|---|---|\n| Muddington Park | rain (0.7) | **mud** patches (4-6 floor-tag blobs): speed ×0.8, acceleration ×0.6, tackles +10%, ball skids; catches -6% in rain; kits get muddier as the match goes on (rig colours mixed toward brown by each player's time in mud and on the ground) |\n| Port Grumble Docks | gusty wind | **wind** that shifts every 15-25 s (strength 0-1, a windsock on the HUD) pushes airborne balls (40 u/s² × strength × `windMult`); **CAPTAIN CLUCKY**, the giant chicken mascot, invades every 50-70 s, runs across on an `E.Path` for about 6 s, bowling over everyone in his way (the carrier drops the ball), chased by the referee |\n| The Furnace | clear night | **flame jets**: grates 32 u inside each touchline (8 a side) erupt in sequences; each glows orange for 1.0 s (the warning), then burns for 1.2 s; anyone within 12 u is TOASTED (stunned 1.2 s, smoking, briefly blackened; a toasted carrier drops the ball); fireworks on every try |\n| The Megadome | thunderstorm (rain 0.9) | **lightning** every 20-30 s: a crackling ring (36 u) warns for 1.4 s at a spot 60-200 u from the ball, then a strike: a flash, thunder, a scorch decal; anyone inside is stunned 1.5 s (drawn as a skeleton for two frames: a shared `build: 'skeleton'` rig drawn in their place) and a carrier inside drops the ball |\n\n`hazardEvery` (×1.0) scales every hazard's frequency; 0 turns them off.\n\n### 7.19 AI\n\nBoth CPU teams and the CPU teammates of humans run the same brain; difficulty and the team's style (§9.1) change its\nnumbers, never its logic. Shapes are recomputed every 0.25 s per team (staggered); decisions every 0.15 s plus the\nreaction delay.\n\n- **Attack shape** (team in possession; carrier at `(cx, cy)`, attacking direction `d`): six support slots in a\n  staggered line behind the carrier, three each side: slot k at `(cx - d × (18 + 10k), cy ∓ 44k)` (spacing 44 to the\n  open side, 36 to the blind side), clamped 20 u inside touch. Forwards take the k = 1 slots, backs the wider ones, the\n  wing the widest open-side slot; then nearest-first; a reassignment needs a 20 u improvement (hysteresis). Supporters\n  never stand in front of the carrier (they check stride to stay 6 u behind). After a line break they turbo.\n- **Defence shape:** a line at `cx + d × 30` facing the attack (behind the offside line when there is one), defenders\n  paired to attackers by y order (\"man on man drift\") so the line slides with the attack; the nearest defender by\n  intercept time is the **tackler** (aims at the carrier's predicted position), the second the **cover** (20 u behind\n  and inside); the **sweeper** (the wing or fly-half) sits 140 u deep at `lerp(cy, CY, .5)` to field kicks, and joins\n  the line when the ball is within 200 u of his try line. With six men (sin bin) the line spaces wider.\n- **Tackler decisions:** in range and facing, after `aiReaction`: try with `0.6 + 0.3 × aggression`; a big hit if POW\n  ≥ 7 or aggression ≥ 0.6 and the carrier is coming head on (charging from 40 u out); a dive tackle when chasing a\n  faster carrier from 18-30 u behind; cheap shots on the nearest support runner when the referee is not looking, with\n  the team's `cheapShots` rate.\n- **Carrier decisions** (CPU carriers, and the human's teammates when they have the ball): score each option and take\n  the best, with noise by difficulty: run forward (space in a 30° cone ahead), pass to each legal receiver (his space\n  minus defenders near the lane), sidestep (a tackler committing within 22 u: 25% × skill), fend (a tackler within 16 u\n  and POW ≥ 6: 40%), kick (deep in his own 22 under pressure: to touch; behind a flat line with a fast chaser: grubber\n  or chip; the last 20 s, trailing by 3 or less, in range: drop goal), dive in the in-goal (or run to the posts when no\n  defender is within 60 u). Steer toward the widest gap in the defensive line; keep 20 u inside touch; turbo in space\n  and when racing to the line; keep 30% of the tank.\n- **Loose ball:** the two nearest from each team chase its predicted rest point; the rest keep their shape.\n- **Kicks:** the receiving team's nearest (or the sweeper) goes to the landing marker, a second supports; the kicking\n  team's two fastest chase. (There is no offside in open play in this game; this is deliberate.)\n- **Set pieces:** see each set piece above. CPU kick-offs aim short and contestable, 120-200 u past halfway toward a\n  touchline. CPU penalty choice: kick at goal within 300 u when the score is close or late; kick to touch from far; tap\n  & go within 50 u of the line or when trailing late.\n- **Difficulty** (the player's Settings choice shifts each cup opponent one step):\n\n| | Rookie | Pro | Legend |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `aiReaction` | 0.40 s | 0.25 s | 0.14 s |\n| Tackle chance | -0.12 | 0 | +0.08 |\n| `cpuMash` | 6/s | 9/s | 12/s |\n| Decision noise | 0.35 | 0.20 | 0.08 |\n| Interception × | 0.5 | 1 | 1.5 |\n| Scrum timing σ | 0.25 s | 0.12 s | 0.06 s |\n| Early engagement | 8% | 3% | 0% |\n| Lineout read | 0.25 | 0.35 | 0.45 |\n\n### 7.20 Instant replay\n\n- A ring buffer keeps the `MatchState` of the last 5 s at 60 Hz (every other step).\n- Triggers: monster hits, supers, tries that came from a run of 200 u or more or beat a man, drop goals, pushover\n  tries, interception tries; at most one replay in 30 s (tries always). Setting: Replays Big moments (default) / All\n  tries / Off.\n- Playback: the window from 2.5 s before to 1 s after the event, at 0.5x, through the normal presentation (states fed\n  to the rigs), camera at zoom 1.35 on the key actor, letterbox bars, \"INSTANT REPLAY\" in the corner, Barry: \"Let's see\n  that again!\"; any button skips. After a try it plays in the celebration, before the conversion. Never in AI Hub\n  sessions.\n\n### 7.21 Stats and the Player of the Match\n\nPer team: possession % (time holding the ball), territory % (ball in the opponents' half), tries, conversions\nmade/attempted, penalties conceded, tackles made/missed, big hits, monster hits, metres carried (`units / 10.24`), line\nbreaks, turnovers won, offloads, cards. Player of the Match (winning side): tries × 10 + monster hits × 4 + tackles + metres\n/ 10 + line breaks × 3 + turnovers × 3. Results show four tiles: TRIES, BIG HITS, METRES, POSSESSION.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Modes, scenes and flow\n\n```\nboot → title ─(10 s idle)→ attract ─(any input)→ title\n         │ PRESS START\n         ▼\n       menu ─(10 s idle)→ attract\n         ├─ MEGA CUP ─→ cup hub ─→ story (prologue) → training (optional) → story (pre-match) → [join] → match\n         │                 ▲                                                                        │\n         │                 └──── results (win: next round; loss: CONTINUE? 10 s) ←───────────────────┘\n         │                 final won → story (trophy) → story (third half) → credits → title\n         ├─ EXHIBITION → join → setup (teams, venue, weather, time, halves) → match → results → rematch | menu\n         ├─ TRAINING GROUND → drill list → match (drill) → next drill | list\n         ├─ RECORDS → three tables (attract-style)\n         ├─ SETTINGS → the standard settings screen (game.menu('settings'))\n         └─ ABOUT & CREDITS → five pages\nAI Hub session: boot → card (the game's own) → match (session) → end overlay (no title, no menus)\n```\n\n| Scene | What it is |\n|---|---|\n| `title` | Night stadium under floodlights behind the logo; two Mudlarks passing a ball in the background (the real presentation, a tiny CPU loop); \"PRESS START\" (or the touch-only message); E.Arcade drives the idle cycle (`idle: 10`) |\n| `menu` | BigMenu (scale 2): MEGA CUP (CONTINUE if a cup save exists), EXHIBITION, TRAINING GROUND, RECORDS, SETTINGS, ABOUT & CREDITS; a one-line description of the focused item; 10 s idle → attract |\n| `attract` | the match scene with `{ attract: true }` (§13) |\n| `cup` | the bracket: four big cards (ROUND ONE, QUARTER-FINAL, SEMI-FINAL, GRAND FINAL) with the opponent crest, venue, result or NEXT or LOCKED; PLAY NEXT MATCH, TRAINING, TEAM SHEET (seven portraits with nickname and role; ✕ on one shows its five stat bars), BACK |\n| `story` | runs one `E.Story` node on a staged set (clubhouse, pitch-side, tunnel, podium; §9.3), then `go(next)`; ✕ turns pages, △ skips the scene |\n| `join` | \"PRESS START TO JOIN\" (pads) or 2 (keyboard right half); each seat moves left/right to HOME, AWAY or CPU; in the cup only HOME; ✕ ready; up to 4 |\n| `setup` | Exhibition: HOME and AWAY team cards (left/right to change; crest, name, three bars: SPEED, POWER, SKILL), VENUE (picture card), WEATHER (Venue default / Clear / Rain / Wind / Storm), TIME (Day / Dusk / Night), HALVES (2-5 min), SUDDEN DEATH (On/Off); PLAY |\n| `match` | the match (pausable); data `{ home, away, venue, weather, time, half, cup, drill, attract, session, seed }` |\n| `results` | the score with crests, PLAYER OF THE MATCH (portrait, two stats), four stat tiles, CONTINUE; a record set → initials (E.Arcade letter wheel) |\n| `training` | the nine drills as big cards with a tick when done; ✕ plays one |\n| `records` | three tables, one a page: BIGGEST WINS (margin), MOST TRIES IN A MATCH, BIGGEST HIT (metres flown); initials |\n| `about` | five pages (§20); L1/R1 or left/right turns them |\n| `credits` | rolls over the third half (§9.3), then the title |\n| `card` | the AI Hub card (§15.2) |\n\n**Deep links** (for `tools/check.mjs`, filmstrips and screenshots, read from `location.hash` at start as the kits do):\n`#title`, `#menu`, `#cup`, `#training`, `#training/<n>`, `#match` (an Exhibition with the defaults), `#match/<venue>`,\n`#attract`, `#records`, `#about`, `#credits`, `#card` (the session card with made-up players, for screenshots only).\n\n**Pause menu** (standard, adjusted): Resume, RESTART MATCH, DEV MODE, Settings, Controls, Full screen, Quit to title\n(none of these in a session, §15.2).\n\n**Saves:** `game.saves` with `menu: { saves: false }` (no manual save slots: arcade); the cup autosaves at the cup hub\nand after each match: `{ round, results: [[home, away]], seeds, difficulty, stats }` with `place: 'MEGA CUP'`, `level:\nround`. CONTINUE on the menu loads `game.saves.latest()`. Records and unlocks in `E.store` (`thugby:records`,\n`thugby:unlocks`). Winning the cup unlocks the MEGACORP MAULERS in Exhibition and a BIG HEADS cheat (Settings, Game).","numLines":420,"startLine":475,"totalLines":1679}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01GmiAM5m8gfWXduyq71z4CL","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
