{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Biu5yJpi6UfZ5wetQiFdnU","type":"tool_result","content":"789:    /** glyphs: the gamepad's button symbols for label(): 'auto' (from the controller's name) | 'xbox' | 'playstation' |\n792:    this.glyphs = 'auto'; this.rumbleScale = .6; this.padLost = false;\n895:   *  button by its symbol on the controller in use ('A', '✕', 'B'...; glyphs picks the family) */\n904:  /** the controller family whose symbols label() shows: glyphs, or with glyphs 'auto' the one its name says */\n906:    if (this.glyphs && this.glyphs !== 'auto') return this.glyphs;\n1302: * 6. PIXEL FONT  3x5 glyphs for in-world numbers and labels\n1354:  normal: { glyphs: parseFont(G57), h: 7, desc: 2, gap: 1, space: 3, upper: false },\n1355:  tiny: { glyphs: parseFont(GLYPHS), h: 5, desc: 0, gap: 2, space: 3, upper: true, mono: 3 }\n1369:  _glyph(f, ch) { return f.glyphs[f.upper ? ch.toUpperCase() : ch] || f.glyphs[ch.toUpperCase()] || f.glyphs['?']; },\n1426:   * Big logo text for title screens: scaled glyphs with a vertical color gradient, an outline and an extruded 3D edge.\n2999:  glyphs: { group: 'Controller', label: 'Button symbols', type: 'select', value: 'auto', options: [['auto', 'Auto'], ['xbox', 'Xbox'], ['playstation', 'PlayStation'], ['nintendo', 'Nintendo'], ['generic', 'Positions']], apply: (g, v) => { g.input.glyphs = v; } },\n---\n45: *    input.label(action) for prompts, and a boot (10c): heavy setup in game.start({ boot: { steps } }) runs behind a\n912:  label(a, device = this.lastDevice) {\n14502:  label() { return 'DAY ' + this.day + '  ' + String(this.hour).padStart(2, '0') + ':' + String(Math.floor(this.minute / 10) * 10).padStart(2, '0'); }\n---\n3657: *    numpad on the right), touch for player 1. game.allowJoin({ max, onJoin }) lets them in: Start on a free pad, or 2 (the\n3686: *  (input, number) as each does. allowJoin(false) closes it (the names split and join are String's and Array's) */\n---\n7472: