{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi3prFiVEFoghhRHoaMs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013xa9k6UrpSa53J8bGtBHMk","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-070011__xa7e588/work && cat > exit-interview.json <<'EOF'\n{\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\"date\": \"2026-11-04 07:00:11\", \"source\": \"rugby (over the top arcade style)\", \"plan\": \"PLAN.md (a THUGBY TURBO plan by another model, used as reference; title re-drawn)\", \"genre\": \"Sports (arcade rugby sevens)\", \"perspective\": \"three-quarter broadcast camera, pitch left to right\", \"tech\": \"my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff engine, Canvas 2D, Web Audio; no other libraries\", \"artDirection\": \"the engine's pixel look at 320x240 scaled to the screen; 3D skeleton figures; lit night venues\", \"animation\": \"the engine's Humanoid rig and standard poses; no new paired moves\", \"audio\": \"all in code (engine chip synth): music, effects, babble commentary; no files\", \"online\": \"none\", \"testing\": \"headless suite of 158 checks plus screenshots\", \"research\": \"the plan, the handoff API card and the sports kit\", \"environment\": \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux under WSL2; headless Chromium for screenshots\", \"model\": \"Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\", \"usage\": \"unknown\"},\n  \"testingFeedback\": [\n    \"About 12 real bugs and about a dozen harness problems. Three were game-breaking: the results screen did not open after the first match of a session; the dev panel freeze stayed on after closing; a penalty kicked to touch froze the ball.\",\n    \"Three game-breaking issues (see the first answer).\",\n    \"The scripted whole-cup playthrough with an autopilot in the human's seat: it caught the results and cup bugs.\",\n    \"The tackle success test over 400 tries: it checked a formula against itself and passed on the first run.\"\n  ],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\n    \"The scene, input, TileMap, Humanoid and Dialog APIs did what the API card said.\",\n    \"Stuck: saves use localStorage, which does not exist in Node, so headless tests needed an in-memory stand-in. Also the Dialog's voice blip is per page, so per-letter babble needed game code.\",\n    \"Built by hand: the rugby simulation, set pieces, the CPU brain, the HUD, commentary and babble, and the dev panel.\",\n    \"Hardest: TileMap wall heights and camera framing, and drawing rigs in the right order over the stands.\",\n    \"No engine patches were made.\",\n    \"I would change one thing: a headless Dialog and menu test API, so UI flows could be checked without a browser.\"\n  ],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\n    \"The plan is very thorough and says exactly what each system should do, with numbers.\",\n    \"The plan and TASK.md disagree on the title and file names; TASK.md has to win, and the plan's scope is far beyond one session.\",\n    \"Writing a full sports sim with set pieces, AI and tests in one pass was the hardest part.\",\n    \"Ship a smaller first milestone with a clear cut list, and say which features are required for the demo.\"\n  ],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"SMASHBY\",\n    \"tagline\": \"Big hits, bigger hair, seven a side\",\n    \"description\": \"Over-the-top arcade rugby sevens: turbo runs, big hits, a referee who only sees some of it, and a pub team's run at the Mega Cup.\",\n    \"type\": \"Game\",\n    \"genre\": \"Sports\",\n    \"source\": \"rugby\",\n    \"series\": \"\",\n    \"players\": \"1\",\n    \"controls\": \"Left stick or WASD run, R2 or Shift turbo, Cross or Space tackle or step, Circle or C kick, L1/R1 or Q/E pass, Triangle or R super\",\n    \"tags\": [\"sports\", \"arcade\", \"comedy\", \"pixel art\", \"3d\"]\n  }\n}\nEOF\npython3 -c \"import json;d=json.load(open('exit-interview.json'));print('parses; keys', list(d.keys()), 'tp', len(d['testingFeedback']), 'ef', len(d['engineFeedback']), 'pf', len(d['promptFeedback']))\"\ncd Smashby-Rugby-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-070011 && rm -f test/dbg.mjs test/probe.py test/probe2.py test/human-start.mjs test/flow.mjs && rm -rf _clone && ls","description":"Write the exit interview, verify it parses, and clean up scratch files"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3286,"cache_read_input_tokens":440620,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3286},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5f6aeda2-f9ed-42d4-a150-3a2efde4ea9e","uuid":"cd366352-2919-4e65-a649-9ba06710ed38","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:31:25.757Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi3pqtdzvfrhZjtg3CA3","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_013xa9k6UrpSa53J8bGtBHMk":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-070011__xa7e588/work && cat > exit-interview.json <<'EOF'\n{\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\"date\": \"2026-11-04 07:00:11\", \"source\": \"rugby (over the top arcade style)\", \"plan\": \"PLAN.md (a THUGBY TURBO plan by another model, used as reference; title re-drawn)\", \"genre\": \"Sports (arcade rugby sevens)\", \"perspective\": \"three-quarter broadcast camera, pitch left to right\", \"tech\": \"my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff engine, Canvas 2D, Web Audio; no other libraries\", \"artDirection\": \"the engine's pixel look at 320x240 scaled to the screen; 3D skeleton figures; lit night venues\", \"animation\": \"the engine's Humanoid rig and standard poses; no new paired moves\", \"audio\": \"all in code (engine chip synth): music, effects, babble commentary; no files\", \"online\": \"none\", \"testing\": \"headless suite of 158 checks plus screenshots\", \"research\": \"the plan, the handoff API card and the sports kit\", \"environment\": \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux under WSL2; headless Chromium for screenshots\", \"model\": \"Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\", \"usage\": \"unknown\"},\n  \"testingFeedback\": [\n    \"About 12 real bugs and about a dozen harness problems. Three were game-breaking: the results screen did not open after the first match of a session; the dev panel freeze stayed on after closing; a penalty kicked to touch froze the ball.\",\n    \"Three game-breaking issues (see the first answer).\",\n    \"The scripted whole-cup playthrough with an autopilot in the human's seat: it caught the results and cup bugs.\",\n    \"The tackle success test over 400 tries: it checked a formula against itself and passed on the first run.\"\n  ],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\n    \"The scene, input, TileMap, Humanoid and Dialog APIs did what the API card said.\",\n    \"Stuck: saves use localStorage, which does not exist in Node, so headless tests needed an in-memory stand-in. Also the Dialog's voice blip is per page, so per-letter babble needed game code.\",\n    \"Built by hand: the rugby simulation, set pieces, the CPU brain, the HUD, commentary and babble, and the dev panel.\",\n    \"Hardest: TileMap wall heights and camera framing, and drawing rigs in the right order over the stands.\",\n    \"No engine patches were made.\",\n    \"I would change one thing: a headless Dialog and menu test API, so UI flows could be checked without a browser.\"\n  ],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\n    \"The plan is very thorough and says exactly what each system should do, with numbers.\",\n    \"The plan and TASK.md disagree on the title and file names; TASK.md has to win, and the plan's scope is far beyond one session.\",\n    \"Writing a full sports sim with set pieces, AI and tests in one pass was the hardest part.\",\n    \"Ship a smaller first milestone with a clear cut list, and say which features are required for the demo.\"\n  ],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"SMASHBY\",\n    \"tagline\": \"Big hits, bigger hair, seven a side\",\n    \"description\": \"Over-the-top arcade rugby sevens: turbo runs, big hits, a referee who only sees some of it, and a pub team's run at the Mega Cup.\",\n    \"type\": \"Game\",\n    \"genre\": \"Sports\",\n    \"source\": \"rugby\",\n    \"series\": \"\",\n    \"players\": \"1\",\n    \"controls\": \"Left stick or WASD run, R2 or Shift turbo, Cross or Space tackle or step, Circle or C kick, L1/R1 or Q/E pass, Triangle or R super\",\n    \"tags\": [\"sports\", \"arcade\", \"comedy\", \"pixel art\", \"3d\"]\n  }\n}\nEOF\npython3 -c \"import json;d=json.load(open('exit-interview.json'));print('parses; keys', list(d.keys()), 'tp', len(d['testingFeedback']), 'ef', len(d['engineFeedback']), 'pf', len(d['promptFeedback']))\"\ncd Smashby-Rugby-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-070011 && rm -f test/dbg.mjs test/probe.py test/probe2.py test/human-start.mjs test/flow.mjs && rm -rf _clone && ls","description":"Write the exit interview, verify it parses, and clean up scratch files"}}}
